471	74,595,854,1470 - 110,590,175,970 - 640,1080,860,1475	471. Plant of Canada Asarum or Wild-Ginger, in flower.	A creeping rootstock with fibrous roots, sending up two long-stalked kidney-shaped leaves and, between them near the ground, a single short bell-shaped flower.
472	647,988,1181,1460 - 668,1295,790,1462 - 1000,985,1130,1035 - 647,985,830,1085	472 Magnified flower divided lengthwise, and the calyx spread out flat.	The flower cut down the middle, its three pointed calyx lobes spread flat, the stamens and thick style in the centre and the ovary below full of seeds.
473	933,594,1140,1005	473. Flower, with the lobes of the calyx cut away, and the ovary cut across.	Above, the ring of stamens with pointed filaments round the thick style; below, the ovary cut across to show its six cells of seeds.
